  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000121964,
      "SummaryText": "Real Alloy Specification is committed to maintaining a safe work environment for our employees, contractors, visitors and the surrounding public.  The company continues to work closely with outside responders and is actively involved with the Local Emergency Planning Committee (LEPC).  Specification secondary aluminum alloys are produced at the site.  The facility has a Program 3 covered process due on-site storage and use of chlorine to remove magnesium and impurities from the alloys produced.  The general accidental release prevention program and chemical-specific prevention steps: The facility is covered by EPA\u0092s Risk Management Program rule and OSHA\u0092s Process Safety Management rule for the process using chlorine.  The facility implements a combined Process Safety & Risk Management Program that consists of a written management system that complies with both USEPA\u0092s & OSHA\u0092s requirements. The five-year accident history:  The facility has not had incident releases of chlorine in the past five years.  Any release inside the storage building is neutralized by the dry scrubber. The emergency response program:  The facility does not have a HazMat Team in place to offensively respond to releases of chlorine.  An automatic cylinder valve closure will activate if the areas monitor detects significant chlorine. The plant has coordinated emergency response procedures with the Wabash County Emergency Management Agency and is planning to conduct a mock disaster exercise at the site in 2026 or 2027.  In the event of a release which could result in an offsite impact, the Emergency Management Agency will be contacted to alert the general public. Significant improvements to the chlorine system were completed in 2024 with the installation of new chlorine piping, controls and furnace area monitoring for a chlorine release."
    }
  ]
